<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Avmin half yr share post-excepts surges.</title>
<headline>Avmin half yr share post-excepts surges.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended December 31</p>
<p>			 (million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr (cts)</p>
<p>    - post-excepts	   31.9   vs   10.9</p>
<p>    - pre-excepts	    43.6   vs   10.9</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		  10.0   vs    2.6</p>
<p>    Attributable income   116.2   vs   35.04</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     42.70   vs   --</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		  198.03   vs   67.23</p>
<p>    Tax			 72.73   vs   28.71</p>
<p>    Turnover		 735.86   vs   97.14</p>
<p>Full name: Anglovaal Minerals</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said earnings from its diamond interests were expected to remain high in the second half of the year, but may not match the record levels achieved for the first half.</p>
<p>Earnings from its gold division were expected to be weaker due to lower projected gold prices.</p>
<p>Its ferrous metal and coal divisions were also expected to show stronger earnings.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
